        {
          "value": "City Council report: 55 BMR units for very low (50% AMI) and low (80% AMI) income households, deed-restricted in perpetuity at a blended 65% AMI (15% of the 361-unit base count); plus 3 studios at 90% AMI and 2 one-bedrooms at 100% AMI for 10 to 15 years under the East Whisman Bonus FAR program, for 60 affordable units. The Development Agreement gives the City an option to master lease or guarantee 30 to 60 more units as BMR for at least 7 years.",
