    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001101"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City Council report lists the applicant and owner as Jeffrey Stone of WTA Middlefield, LLC. The site holds one occupied two-story office building. The eight-story building totals about 391,775 sq ft with an at-grade one-level podium garage; 29 heritage trees removed.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002228"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Development Agreement with WTA Middlefield, LLC: 4-year term with two optional 2-year extensions ($100,000 and $250,000 fees); $1.1 million community benefit fee (1.41 Bonus FAR, 175,476 sq ft at $6.23/sq ft) payable at final certificate of occupancy; $1.2 million retail tenant improvements; $1.2 million Recreational City Facilities Contribution toward park land within 1,250 feet or Pyramid Park.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002228",
        "SRC-002229"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Second-reading report: council introduced the Development Agreement ordinance 6-0 with one member absent on March 10, 2026; project estimated to raise the City's property tax share from about $18,000 to about $140,000 per year.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002229"
      ]
